Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In this example, you can't. Your initial example specified the items

Bkl1:  items 1 -20
Bkl2: items 11-40 (items 11 to 20 shared with booklet 1)
Bkl3: items 31-50 (items 31 to 40 shared with booklet 2)

with very clear overlap in the item contents. In your new example, if the items are not shared across booklets then you can't properly link the item response information, so you effectively must look at these items/responses as completely distinct.

Phil

